@PolicyApi_HostAddress = http://localhost:5187

### 1. Get a token for Tenant 1 (Acme). Send THIS request first, then send the ones below.
# @name login
POST {{PolicyApi_HostAddress}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": 1
}

### 2. Happy path - customer 1 (Alice) policy, scoped to Tenant 1 -> 200
GET {{PolicyApi_HostAddress}}/api/customers/1/policy
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 3. Expiring policies within 30 days, tenant-scoped -> only Acme policies
GET {{PolicyApi_HostAddress}}/api/policies/expiring?withinDays=30
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 4. Bonus - deterministic expiration-date lookup by policy number -> 200
GET {{PolicyApi_HostAddress}}/api/policies/ACME-1001/expiration-date
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 5. BLOCKED cross-tenant - customer 3 belongs to Tenant 2, so a Tenant 1 token gets 404
GET {{PolicyApi_HostAddress}}/api/customers/3/policy
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 6. No token at all -> 401
GET {{PolicyApi_HostAddress}}/api/policies/expiring

### 7. Negative withinDays -> 400
GET {{PolicyApi_HostAddress}}/api/policies/expiring?withinDays=30
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 8. Get a token for Tenant 2 (Globex). Send this before request 9.
# @name loginT2
POST {{PolicyApi_HostAddress}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": 2
}

### 9. Tenant 2 sees its OWN customer 3 policy -> 200 (the same id Tenant 1 could not see)
GET {{PolicyApi_HostAddress}}/api/customers/3/policy
Authorization: Bearer {{loginT2.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 10. Token request for an unknown tenant -> 404
POST {{PolicyApi_HostAddress}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": 999
}
